{"kind":"finding","id":"F-ledger-career-029-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/KerbalExperienceFacetTests.cs","line":506,"method":"Reassert_SkipsAKerbalTheRosterDoesNotHaveInsteadOfCreatingOne","category":"T1","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/KerbalsModule.cs:1951; deleting the rosterEntries == null skip so the absent kerbal falls through to AppendCareerLogEntries -> this cell stays green, because the test's own facade refuses unknown names without recording at KerbalExperienceFacetTests.cs:564","what_it_asserts":"ApplyToRoster appends no career-log entries for a kerbal the roster facade does not know, instead of creating one.","why_weak":"The asserted list can never be non-empty: RecordingRosterFacade records appends only for names in KnownKerbals (:556, :564), and the module row is for the unknown 'Ghost Kerman'. A create regression is invisible too, since TryCreateGeneratedStandIn returns false and nothing records the call. The cell asserts a mock it configured.","proposed_action":"Make the fixture honest: have AppendCareerLogEntries record any name (keep a separate refusal switch if needed) and record TryCreateGeneratedStandIn/TryRecreateStandIn calls, then assert no append and no create attempt; the cell then reds if the :1951 skip is dropped or a create is wired into ReassertCareerLogEntries.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
